## 2. Typography

Two-family system, chosen for a back-office/financial-data context rather than a marketing site:

- **Display/UI face:** `Inter` (or system-ui fallback stack: `-apple-system, "Segoe UI", Inter, sans-serif`) — used for all headings, nav, buttons, labels. Chosen for its neutrality and excellent legibility at small sizes in dense UI, not for personality — this product's personality comes from the status-color system and layout discipline, not display type.
- **Tabular/data face:** `"IBM Plex Mono"` (or `ui-monospace` fallback) — used specifically for **numeric data**: salary figures, scores, percentages, dates in tables, employee/candidate IDs. Monospacing numerals is what makes columns of payroll figures or KPI scores actually scannable at a glance — this is the deliberate, subject-specific typographic choice for this brief.

```css
:root {
  --font-ui: "Inter", -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  --font-data: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;

  --text-xs: 0.75rem;    /* 12px — table meta, captions */
  --text-sm: 0.8125rem;   /* 13px — table body, secondary labels */
  --text-base: 0.9375rem;  /* 15px — default body/UI text */
  --text-lg: 1.125rem;      /* 18px — section headings */
  --text-xl: 1.5rem;         /* 24px — page titles */
  --text-2xl: 1.875rem;        /* 30px — dashboard hero numbers only */

  --weight-regular: 400;
  --weight-medium: 500;
  --weight-semibold: 600;
}
```

**Rule:** any cell displaying a number (currency, score, count, percentage) uses `--font-data`. Any label, name, or descriptive text uses `--font-ui`. This split alone does most of the work of making tables feel precise rather than generic.

---

## 3. Spacing & Layout

```css
:root {
  --space-1: 4px;
  --space-2: 8px;
  --space-3: 12px;
  --space-4: 16px;
  --space-5: 24px;
  --space-6: 32px;
  --space-8: 48px;

  --radius-sm: 4px;    /* inputs, badges, buttons */
  --radius-md: 6px;     /* cards, modals */
  --radius-none: 0px;    /* tables — sharp edges reinforce the data-tool feel, not soft cards */

  --sidebar-width: 240px;
  --content-max-width: 1440px;
  --table-row-height: 44px;
}
```

**Layout shell (all authenticated pages):**

```
┌────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│            │  Top bar: page title, breadcrumb, actions │
│  Sidebar   ├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  (nav,     │                                           │
│  module    │  Page content (max-width 1440px,         │
│  icons +   │  centered, --space-6 padding)             │
│  labels)   │                                           │
│            │                                           │
└────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- Sidebar: fixed width, grouped by module (Job Descriptions, CV Screening, Attendance, Payroll, KPI, Admin Panel), collapses to icon-only under 1024px viewport.
- Top bar: always shows current page title + a short breadcrumb for nested pages (e.g. `Job Descriptions / Backend Engineer / Candidates`), primary action button (e.g. "New Job Description") right-aligned.

