## 4. Core Components

### Status Badge
Pill-shaped, `--radius-sm`, background = the `-bg` variant of the status color, text = the solid status color, `--text-xs`, `--weight-medium`, uppercase, letter-spacing 0.02em. Always paired with the status rail on the containing row/card — badge and rail must use the same semantic status, never independently colored.

### Status Rail (signature element)
A 3px-wide colored bar on the left edge of: table rows (via `border-left`), cards, and list items. Color = the row/card's primary status via the semantic mapping in §1. This is the one consistent visual thread across every module — implement once as a shared CSS utility/component (`components/ui/StatusRail` or a `data-status` attribute + CSS), never reimplemented per module.

### Table
- Header row: `--color-surface-alt` background, `--text-xs` `--weight-semibold` uppercase labels, sticky on scroll for long lists.
- Body rows: `--table-row-height`, hover state = `--color-surface-alt`, `--radius-none`, hairline `--color-border` bottom on each row (no full grid lines — horizontal only, keeps it calm).
- Numeric columns right-aligned, `--font-data`.
- Every table that maps to a paginated API response uses the shared `components/ui/Pagination` footer.

### Card
`--color-surface` background, `--radius-md`, `--color-border` 1px border (no shadow by default — shadows reserved for modals/dropdowns only, to keep the flat back-office feel), `--space-4` internal padding. Used for dashboard summary tiles, employee/candidate detail panels.

### Button
- Primary: `--color-accent` background, `--color-text-inverse` text, `--radius-sm`, `--weight-medium`, hover → `--color-accent-hover`.
- Secondary: transparent background, `--color-border-strong` border, `--color-text-primary` text.
- Destructive (reject candidate, delete): `--color-status-critical` text on transparent, `--color-status-critical-bg` on hover — never a filled red button, this is an admin tool where destructive actions should require a confirm step, not just be visually loud.
- Approve/positive actions (approve payroll, shortlist candidate): filled `--color-status-positive`.

### Form Field
Label (`--text-sm`, `--weight-medium`, `--color-text-secondary`) above input. Input: `--color-surface` bg, `--color-border-strong` border, `--radius-sm`, focus state = 2px `--color-accent` outline (never remove focus outlines — keyboard accessibility matters in an internal tool used all day). Error state: `--color-status-critical` border + inline message below field in `--text-xs` critical color.

### Modal
`--color-surface`, `--radius-md`, drop shadow (`0 8px 24px rgba(16,24,40,0.12)`) — the one place shadow is used, to visually lift it above the flat page. Max-width 560px for simple forms, 800px for detail/review modals.

### Score / KPI Visual
A horizontal bar (not a gauge/donut — bars compare more legibly in a list of many rows) showing actual vs target, using the KPI status semantic colors. Numeric value in `--font-data` to the right of the bar, always shown alongside the visual (never color-only — accessibility, and precision matters for payroll-adjacent decisions).

